# scene_service — COVERAGE ANCHORS, not bug repros.
#
# This target found no bugs in SceneService: 6 000 explore cases passed clean.
# That is a result, not an absence of one — but it means the corpus cannot be
# "every bug ever found" the way the other lanes' corpora are. These seeds are
# pinned because they exercise the paths the properties depend on: multi-entity
# scenes, real cooked meshes resolving through AssetService, EntityId collision
# reassignment, deep parent chains, and the truncated-file rejection path.
#
# What proves they BITE is mutation, re-runnable at any time:
#   - remove the destruct() in unloadScene  -> "load/unload LEAKED" on seed 1
#   - swap safeReparent for a raw child_of  -> SIGABRT inside flecs'
#     childof-depth recursion, which the lane reports as a failed test
#
# The second is worth stating precisely: the cycle is caught by flecs aborting
# before the ancestor-walk assertion is ever reached. The walk still earns its
# place — it covers a cycle that flecs tolerates — but it is not what fired.
